{% extends 'base.html.twig' %}

{% block title %}About extdir{% endblock %}
{% block canonical %}<link rel="canonical" href="{{ url('about') }}">{% endblock %}
{% block meta_description %}What extdir is, who runs it, and where its data comes from.{% endblock %}

{% block body %}
<div class="wrap page">
    <div class="page-head">
        <h1>About extdir</h1>
        <p>A community-run directory of open-source Shopware 6 extensions.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="prose">
        <p>
            {{ total }} extensions, indexed with the Shopware versions each declares support for
            and when its code was last touched. Independent project, no connection to Shopware AG,
            not a replacement for the Shopware Store. "Shopware" is used descriptively.
        </p>

        <h2>What it is not</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>No payments, listings for sale, or advertising.</li>
            <li>No proprietary extensions.</li>
            <li>No accounts, tracking, or cookies.</li>
            <li>No editorial placement. <a href="{{ path('ranking') }}">Ranking is algorithmic and published.</a></li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Data</h2>
        <p>
            Packages from Packagist, by Composer type. Repository activity from the GitHub API.
            Compatibility is read from the <code>shopware/core</code> constraint the maintainer
            declared, not from a test, so entries say "declares support for" and open-ended
            constraints are shown as less certain.
        </p>

        <h2>Licences</h2>
        <p>
            No licence file means all rights reserved, so those are linked and badged, never
            mirrored. Copyleft is labelled separately from MIT-style.
        </p>

        <h2>Who runs it</h2>
        <p>
            <a href="https://runio.dev" rel="noopener">runio.dev</a>, non-commercial. Contact
            details in the <a href="{{ path('imprint') }}">imprint</a>. The maintainer publishes
            Shopware extensions too: indexed like any other, badged, no ranking preference.
        </p>

        <h2>Open source</h2>
        <p>
            The code is public at <a href="https://github.com/extdir" rel="noopener">github.com/extdir</a>,
            so you can check how the data was produced.
        </p>

        <h2>Found a mistake?</h2>
        <p>
            Entries are generated automatically and some will be wrong. The
            <a href="{{ path('takedown') }}">takedown policy</a> covers corrections and removal.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>
{% endblock %}
